Alembic migrations for the CRM backend.

## Why we have both Alembic AND self-written startup migrations in main.py

`main.py` already runs ~30 idempotent `CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS` /
`ALTER TABLE … ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS` blocks at FastAPI startup.
Those are safe to keep — they bootstrap a fresh DB without needing
Alembic to be present.

Going forward, EVERY schema change goes through Alembic instead.
Versioned, reviewable, reversible — `alembic downgrade -1` rolls
back the most recent migration if the new code is rolled back.

## Day-to-day commands

```
# Apply pending migrations
python -m alembic upgrade head

# Roll back the last applied migration
python -m alembic downgrade -1

# Show current revision
python -m alembic current

# Generate a new (empty) revision skeleton
python -m alembic revision -m "add color column to products"

# Render SQL for a migration without running it (review-only)
python -m alembic upgrade head --sql > migration.sql
```

## Connection URL

Comes from `.env` (same as main.py). `alembic/env.py` reads
`DB_HOST` / `DB_PORT` / `DB_USER` / `DB_PASSWORD` / `DB_NAME` and
builds a SQLAlchemy URL — no need to edit `alembic.ini`.

## Marking an existing DB at baseline

For a DB that already has the schema (pre-Alembic deployments):

    python -m alembic stamp head

This writes `alembic_version` table without running any migrations.
After that, `python -m alembic upgrade head` is a no-op until a new
revision is added.
